  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Job: crew-retrain (Breakroom profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice).",
  "asked": "# Job: crew-retrain (Breakroom profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice). GO given. Book this run on **Landin' Lenny** (agent-swarm card: stats, cost, chat) as the first retrained all-rounder. ## Rules (already in _claude/rules/RULES.md on the hub) - Every agent is an all-rounder: can do every kind of work (feature builds, landing, site checks, UI screenshots, walkthroughs, banner cleanup, listener QA, and any job type added later). - RETRAIN, DON'T FIRE: Brett said \"We can't afford to fire them.\" Keep every agent's name, card, history, chat and pay. Nobody is removed. - Every headless session is assigned to a named agent BEFORE it starts and booked on that agent's card. No anonymous sessions. - Agent pay starts at minimum wage when the Breakroom is finished; raises earned only (HR machinery stays shelved). Vinnie flagged for mistakes, no raise. ## Crew (from `node framework/cli/agent-job.mjs list`) Reel Rhonda (amberx-walkthrough), Janitor Joey (banner-cleanup), Landin' Lenny (land-build), Ping Paulie (site-check), Snap Sully (ui-screenshots), Earl the Ear (listener-qa). Vinnie is axHub's approval bot, not part of this swarm; leave him as is. ## Steps - s0 Register in the Breakroom profile via the orchestrator CLI (id `crew-retrain`) + banner entry. - s1 Job model: job-type@1 assets declare required skills instead of a single owner; agents carry a skill list; give all six agents every skill (all job types). Keep a 'home' job per agent as a preference only (used for tie-breaks), not exclusivity. - s2 New job type `feature-build` (any feature/fix build launched through vps.build_start / deploy/claude-headless.sh / orchestrator) and `ops-fix`; all agents can take them. - s3 Router: pick any on-duty agent under budget, preferring home job then least busy; never route to nobody when someone is free. - s4 Every launcher requires an agent: deploy/claude-headless.sh and the build_start path take `AXF_AGENT` (refuse or auto-assign via the router if missing, and record it); tmux session name and log include the agent; cost/stats/chat booked on the agent. Add an `--agent` flag to agent-job.mjs and a helper `agent-job.mjs assign <build-name>` to attach an already-running/finished build. - s5 Back-assign today's headless builds to the crew (round-robin by the router) and book them on their cards: orch-live-sync, notes-vault, headless-tabs, whats-new-banner, amberx-backup-fix, kill-patches-pilot, theme-veto-pass, axhub-veto-pass, plugin-commands-auto, pass-all, axhub-pass-all, banners-one (stopped), land-everything (Landin' Lenny). List who got what in the report. - s6 Breakroom UI: each agent's card shows all skills, home job, current job; roster shows who's free. - s7 Tests, check-theme/check-controls, lifecycle, report `_claude/builds/reports/crew-retrain.md`, THREADS.md, PR (land-everything is landing PRs; add a note so it picks this up last). Mark steps done through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
